{
  "date": "2026-10-25",
  "scope": "Actual reference field selection and complete ordered manifest child/digest binding, used by native ClosureReader. Graph-domain/context and native authenticated Reader/serializer/SHA/namespace correspondence remain open.",
  "runtime_changes": "ClosureReader calls closure_node::{kind,segment,path,children}; manifest/index read order, array validation before hashing, records-before-dependencies ordering, error categories, hashing and cloning are preserved. Field lookup uses the existing verified object-iteration helper instead of serde map lookup. Executable lookup changes have no zero-overhead claim; no new performance campaign.",
  "properties": {
    "closure_node::{kind,segment,path}": "Exact manifest-presence precedence and nested/direct segment and string path selection. Invalid shape cannot be silently accepted.",
    "closure_node::{array,append,children}": "Both arrays must exist before digest calls. Success contains every record followed by every dependency, including duplicates. Each key matches original canonical content under Digest; each clone preserves content and all finite-depth observations. Failures return no partial successful list; append preserves an existing prefix on success.",
    "closure_node::{complete_keys,graph_binding}": "Ordered keyed output has exactly the original successor key set and satisfies closure::bound when graph key interpretation and domain inclusion are supplied. These premises are not proved for the native graph context."
  },
  "boundaries": [
    "Digest success is a stable function of canonical Value content. Actual crate::digest serializer/SHA correspondence remains an explicit straw adapter obligation; this does not verify SHA or assume collision resistance as a new theorem.",
    "Existing Value access/clone/iteration and String library contracts remain; no additional library primitive or omitted straw proof body was added.",
    "Native authenticated manifest decoding/index checks, namespace resolution, root admission, graph/cache context, catalog locking and complete retain/release/GC correspondence remain unproved.",
    "This closes a per-node field/child construction portion of the dependency item, not the complete TODO item. No new production bug is claimed."
  ],
